{#-
  Schema names are taken LITERALLY.

  dbt ships this macro so that a `+schema: silver` config becomes
  `<target.schema>_silver` — deliberately, so two developers pointed at the
  same warehouse build into separate schemas.

  A migrated estate needs the opposite. Its schemas are not suffixes somebody
  chose; they are the names the legacy system used, the names the landing DDL
  creates, and the names every downstream consumer already references. Left
  concatenated, `+schema: SILVER_SCHEMA` would build ANALYTICS_SILVER_SCHEMA
  and nothing would find it.

  The cost is that developer isolation now has to come from the PROFILE — give
  each developer their own database (or their own set of schemas) in
  profiles.yml, because it can no longer come from the schema suffix.
-#}
{% macro generate_schema_name(custom_schema_name, node) -%}
    {%- if custom_schema_name is none -%}
        {{ target.schema }}
    {%- else -%}
        {{ custom_schema_name | trim }}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
